# Governed CVE waiver list for the InnBucks middleware image scan.
#
# RULES (a waiver without all three is a review failure):
#   * every entry carries: the CVE id, an owner, a one-line reason, and a
#     review-by date — as a comment directly above the id
#   * prefer fixing/upgrading over waiving; a waiver is a scheduled debt,
#     not a dismissal
#   * remove entries at their review date or renew them consciously
#
# The Release workflow scans CRITICAL/HIGH before it pushes, so a red gate
# blocks publication rather than reporting after the fact.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STALE-BRANCH WARNING (2026-09-02): the entries below were written against
# Alpine 3.23 with libexpat 2.8.1-r0 / p11-kit 0.25.5-r2. The base image has
# since moved — eclipse-temurin:21-jre-alpine now ships **Alpine 3.24.1 with
# libexpat 2.8.3-r0** — which is exactly the base-image bump the original note
# named as the exit condition for deleting these.
#
# They are RENEWED rather than deleted only because deletion is unverified from
# here: a waiver for an already-fixed CVE is inert, but deleting one that is
# still live turns the Release gate red on the next merge. Settle it with one
# command against the CURRENT base and delete whatever no longer applies:
#
#     docker run --rm eclipse-temurin:21-jre-alpine \
#       sh -c 'apk update >/dev/null 2>&1; apk policy libexpat p11-kit'
#
# Expectation: the two libexpat entries are superseded by 2.8.3-r0 and should
# go; p11-kit is unknown and needs the output above before anyone touches it.
#
# NOTE these are NOT the CVEs that failed the gate on 2026-09-02 — those were
# CVE-2026-66046 / CVE-2026-76641 against 2.8.3-r0, which have a fix IN branch
# (2.8.4-r0) and were therefore fixed by bumping ALPINE_SECURITY_REFRESH in the
# Dockerfile, not waived. Waiving a fixable CVE is what the rules above forbid.
#
# owner: mpofuslim
# review by: 2026-10-31

# libexpat 2.8.1-r0 — handler call-depth tracking (56131) and copyString
# integer overflow (56408). Reached only via native XML parsing; this service
# parses JSON over HTTP and does not feed untrusted XML to expat, so the
# exposure is indirect at worst. Not a dismissal — revisit at the date above.
CVE-2026-56131
CVE-2026-56408

# p11-kit 0.25.5-r2 — NULL dereference via C_DeriveKey with specific NULL
# parameters. Requires a PKCS#11 token path; the middleware uses JKS/PKCS12
# files for TLS trust and no hardware/softoken PKCS#11 module.
CVE-2026-2100
